day9 before task1 i should know below
     - "apply" (args passed as an [] ), "call" (args listed individually)
     - on both "apply" and "call", we call them on function 
     - "bind" also called on "function" as well, but it returns a  new function

Syntax: apply
- func.apply(thisArg, [argsArray])

Syntax: call
- func.call(thisArg, arg1, arg2, ...)

Eg:
            
function greet(greeting, punctuation) {
  console.log(greeting, this.name, punctuation);
}

const person = {
  name: "Manju",
};

greet.call(person, "Hello", "!"); // call: 
                                        // invoke immediately
                                        // arguments passed individually. Prints 'Hello Manju !'


greet.apply(person, ["Hi", "?"]); // apply: invoke immediately with args as array                                    

// bind: returns a new function
const boundGreet = greet.bind(person, "Hey");//prints Hey Manju !!!
                                               // create a new function and invoke later

boundGreet("!!!");

